0,Zangskari language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zangskari_language,"Zangskari (also spelled Zanskari, Zaskari) is an endangered Tibetic language. It is a dialect of the Ladakhi language. It is mostly spoken in the Zanskar region of the Kargil district of Ladakh, India and also by Buddhists in the upper reaches of Lahaul, Himachal Pradesh, and Paddar, Jammu and Kashmir. [2] It is written using the Tibetan script ...",Zangskari,Sino-Tibetan
1,Ladakhi language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ladakhi_language,"Sino-Tibetan · Tibeto-Burman · Tibeto-Kanauri (?). Bodish · Tibetic · Ladakhi–Balti ... Zangskari language, spoken in the Zanskar region of Ladakh. Contents. 1 ...",Zangskari,Sino-Tibetan
2,Zangskari language — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/zangskari_language,"Zangskari employs the Tibetan script in its Uchen (dbu can) variant, a formal printed style derived from the 7th-century Old Tibetan abugida, which has been adapted from Central Tibetan conventions to accommodate Western Tibetic phonological features like those in Ladakhi dialects.",Zangskari,Sino-Tibetan
3,Tibetan music from Ladakh and Zanskar [sound recording],https://searchworks.stanford.edu/view/304382,"Field recordings of folk songs, folk instrumental music, Buddhist chants, and Buddhist ritual instrumental music. Sung probably in Ladakhi.",Zangskari,Sino-Tibetan
4,YouTube MusicZangskari Language Resource - UNT Digital LibrarySKEYOUL MASHUP 2 |singer Tashi Pishu & Stanzin Gyachin ...Endangered Languages Project - Zangskari,https://music.youtube.com/watch?v=2_cAuQWvRlQ,"New tibetan song 2023 Ngayi Monlam by Tenzin Dangsel ft. Lotsetan. བསྟ་འཛིན་དྭངས་གསལ་དང་བློ་ཚེ་བརྟན།. May 28, 2026 · Broadly, there are four dialects of Zangskari: Stod or Upper Zangskari, Zhung or Central Zangskari, Sham or Lower Zangskari, and Lungnak. This music video celebrates the rich cultural heritage of the breathtaking Zanskar Valley, blending traditional folklore and timeless melodies that have been passed down through generations. Information from: “Language in South Asia” . Braj B. Kachru; Yamuna Kachru; S. N. Sridhar (2008) Cambridge University Press. Information from: “Ethnologue: Languages of the World, 16th Edition (2009)” . M. Paul Lewis · SIL International. Information from: “World Oral Literature Project” .",Zangskari,Sino-Tibetan
